  "_comment": [
    "Measured for squirrelscan/repo#1950 on 2026-09-08 by",
    "apps/cli/scripts/template-rule-invariance.ts over two real crawls. A rule is constant when",
    "every member of every MULTI-PAGE template cluster produced an identical verdict under",
    "templateVerdictKey - the WHOLE check (name, status, message, value, expected, items,",
    "details), with only the page's own url and path normalised away.",
    "rule-verdict-scope.test.ts asserts no rule declares verdictScope \"template\" unless it is",
    "constant on BOTH corpora, so a rule whose inputs change and start varying shows up as a",
    "named classification failure rather than as silent fan-out.",
    "The crawls are third-party site content and cannot be checked in, which is why the RESULT",
    "is recorded here. Regenerate with the script above; never from the synthetic bench corpora,",
    "which are built from 1-6 templates and make every rule look constant (#1026)."
  ],
